tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lent-field-needs-a-place.hero:44:14: error[field_lend_escapes]: `.ptr()` lends this field's address to C for the length of one call (§4.19), and a lend may stand only as an argument of a call — here it stands somewhere the pointer outlives the record it points into
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lent-field-needs-a-place.hero:48:24: error[field_lend_needs_a_place]: `.ptr()` lends a field's address to C, so the field must be one this program can still name — here the bytes belong to a value nothing holds
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lent-field-needs-a-place.hero:51:24: error[bad_operand]: `ptr` takes a fixed run of bytes — `i8[N]` or `u8[N]`, found `[u8]`
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lent-field-needs-a-place.hero:57:20: error[field_lend_needs_a_header]: `.ptr()` lends a field's address to C, and it may stand only as an argument of a function declared in an `extern` group — here the callee is this program's own, and no header says whether it writes through the pointer or how far it reads
